sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant N as nginx
    participant MC as MaterialsController
    participant MS as MaterialsService
    participant JS as JobsService
    participant CO as OcrCoordinatorService<br/>(in-API sweep, every 15 s)
    participant OW as API worker endpoints<br/>/api/v1/ocr/workers/:id/*
    participant WK as ocr-worker (standalone or dev)<br/>heartbeat · claim · fetch · extract · submit
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant ST as storage volume

    B->>N: POST /materials/upload (multipart)
    N->>MC: /api/v1/materials/upload
    MC->>MS: store file (local) → material (UPLOADED)
    B->>N: POST /materials/:id/process
    MC->>JS: INSERT jobs (MATERIAL_PROCESS, status='queued')
    Note over JS: MATERIAL_PROCESS is NEVER published to RabbitMQ<br/>(OCR is coordinator-owned).
    MS-->>B: 202 {jobId}

    loop Coordinator sweep (every 15 s)
        CO->>DB: adopt queued MATERIAL_PROCESS jobs
        CO->>DB: material → PROCESSING, job → processing
        CO->>DB: materialize chunk 1 (pages 1..CHUNK_SIZE=10) → ocr_chunks pending
    end

    loop ocr-worker pull loop
        WK->>OW: POST heartbeat {status: idle|processing} (every 10 s)
        WK->>OW: POST claim
        OW->>CO: find oldest pending (or lease-expired) chunk, FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
        CO->>DB: chunk → claimed, claimedBy, leaseExpiresAt (300 s), attempts+1
        OW-->>WK: {chunk: {id, index, startPage, endPage, pageCount, sourceType, sourceId}}
    end

    WK->>OW: GET source/:chunkId
    OW->>ST: read source bytes
    ST-->>WK: file bytes
    WK->>WK: ocr_engine.extract_range(start, end):<br/>PyMuPDF embedded text ≥5 chars/page → else rasterize → PaddleOCR
    alt success
        WK->>OW: POST chunks/:chunkId/result {pages[], text, totalPages?}
        CO->>CO: validate page range against chunk
        CO->>DB: chunk → submitted
        alt totalPages reported > first chunk end
            CO->>DB: materialize chunks 2..ceil(N/10) (missing indexes only)
        end
    else failure
        WK->>OW: POST chunks/:chunkId/fail {error, permanent}
        CO->>CO: attempts below MAX=3 and not permanent → chunk back to pending (retried)
    end

    CO->>DB: all chunks submitted + contiguous pages 1..N ⇒ persist text
    CO->>DB: material → READY, job → completed
    Note over DB: Lease-expired or disabled-worker chunks reclaimed by sweep.<br/>Settled failure → material FAILED and job failed (terminal after 3 attempts).
    B->>B: poll material until READY (OCR pages viewable, corrections allowed)